UNUserNotificationCenter needs a live Activity to schedule, list or remove a request, and records a permission request made without one as denied; it lists pending requests with no trigger or content; a repeating trigger fires once, because NotificationWorker never enqueues the next occurrence; a calendar trigger keeps the instant it was enqueued for when the zone or clock changes; every add looks up earlier versions' work; and every notification posts to one default-importance channel whatever its interruption level or sound. Requests now use the application context; each saves its work data, from which it is listed with its trigger and content, repeated by the worker (calendar triggers at their next wall-clock time) and re-armed by a manifest receiver on TIMEZONE_CHANGED and TIME_SET; replacement and removal end a repeating chain; add returns once WorkManager has queued the work; earlier versions' work is looked up once per process until none is left; and each interruption level and sound has its own channel. Proposed upstream.

